{#
  Stage 2b — rendered entirely from ONE GraphQL response.

  Every value below comes from `device`, which is the result of a single query
  against Nautobot. No REST round-trips, no group_vars, no survey.

  `default()` guards are deliberate: a Config Context need not define every key,
  and a lab device need not have VLANs or descriptions. A template that explodes
  on the first missing optional field is a bad demo in front of 60 people.
#}
hostname {{ device.name }}
!
{% if device.config_context is defined and device.config_context %}
{% for server in device.config_context.get('ntp_servers', []) %}
ntp server {{ server }}
{% endfor %}
!
{% for server in device.config_context.get('dns_servers', []) %}
ip name-server {{ server }}
{% endfor %}
!
{% if device.config_context.get('snmp_community') %}
snmp-server community {{ device.config_context['snmp_community'] }} ro
{% endif %}
{% if device.config_context.get('syslog_host') %}
logging host {{ device.config_context['syslog_host'] }}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
!
{#
  🔴 NEVER RENDER CONFIG FOR THE OUT-OF-BAND PORT.

  Applying intent to the management interface, over the management interface,
  is how you disconnect yourself mid-commit. It happened on 2026-09-02: a stale
  IP left in Nautobot rendered `ip address 172.20.20.2/24` onto leaf2's
  Management0, whose real address is .12. The commit renumbered the interface,
  the SSH session died, `commit` never returned a prompt, and the job failed
  with a 60-second timeout — after the device had already moved.

  The stale IP was the bug and is fixed in seed_nautobot.yml (`state: replace`).
  This guard is the second line of defence: with it, no data error in Nautobot
  can take a device off the network. In front of sixty people that difference
  matters more than the config it would have applied.

  Note `default(false)` — if the GraphQL query ever stops returning mgmt_only,
  this fails OPEN rather than silently skipping every interface and rendering
  an empty intent that looks like "no drift".
#}
{% for intf in device.interfaces | default([]) if not intf.get('mgmt_only', false) %}
interface {{ intf.name }}
{% if intf.description %}
   description {{ intf.description }}
{% else %}
   description managed by Nautobot
{% endif %}
{% for ip in intf.ip_addresses | default([]) %}
   ip address {{ ip.address }}
{% endfor %}
{% if intf.untagged_vlan %}
   switchport access vlan {{ intf.untagged_vlan.vid }}
{% endif %}
{% if intf.tagged_vlans %}
   switchport trunk allowed vlan {{ intf.tagged_vlans | map(attribute='vid') | join(',') }}
{% endif %}
{% if not intf.enabled %}
   shutdown
{% endif %}
!
{% endfor %}
